Package: canofac
Type: Package
Title: Canonical Factorisation for Multiblock Data
Version: 0.7.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohamed", "Hanafi", email = "mohamed.hanafi@oniris-nantes.fr",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Exploratory multiblock methods written in the canonical
    factorisation X_k = U D_k V_k' (Bougeard et al., 2024), where U holds
    the reference components (scores), shared by all blocks, V_k the axes
    (loadings) of block k and D_k a diagonal matrix of pseudo-singular values.
    The package estimates a family of criteria indexed by a power q applied to
    the pseudo-singular values, which includes MAXBET (q = 1), CPCA and MCOA
    (q = 2), CCSWA/ComDim/ACCPS and INDORT (q = 4), with unconstrained or
    orthonormal axes and sequential or simultaneous extraction, and STATIS
    and multiple factor analysis through the weighting of the blocks. It provides
    the trajectories of each block as q varies, an exact leave-one-block-out (LOBO)
    permutation test, block by block, that designates the blocks linked to the reference
    components estimated on the other blocks, with a subspace statistic that
    weights the components by the inertia of the other blocks (restricted RV)
    or equally,
    p-values by permutation, by a gamma approximation with the exact permutation
    moments or by a hybrid of both, schemes for groups of exchangeable rows,
    comparisons with the full RV test and PROTEST, and a set of plots whose
    labels, like the help (cf_help()), are available in English and in French.
    A Python version with the same functions, labels and random number generator
    (same permutations, hence same p-values, for the same seed) is in the
    directory python/ of the source repository.
